descriptions.ten:
Kyrgyzstan is an agrarian country. Agriculture is an important sector of the economy and provides more than 40% of the gross domestic product (GDP). About three million people, or 60% of the country's population, live in rural areas. As a result of the agrarian and land reform, there are 301,935 farms in the republic, which urgently need versatile technicians who know the basics of crop and livestock production, agricultural mechanization and the agrarian economy. The set of disciplines provides a universal education needed by the modern agricultural sector in a market economy.

Practical training takes place on farms in Kyrgyzstan and at agricultural enterprises in Germany.

After graduation, graduates can:

— carry out marketing planning and keep accounts and reports for farms and other agricultural enterprises;

— work on and manage their own farm;

— work for the Rural Advisory Service and local administration.
